{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cranial-sulfur-peafowl","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n`rebar reopen <child>` moves a closed ticket to open but does NOT cascade to its still-closed parent(s). Combined with the close-time open-children guard (which only blocks closing a parent that has open children), this lets the store reach an invalid state: a CLOSED parent with an OPEN/in_progress child.\n\nObserved while closing epic e215-ab23-ed6a-4791 properly: after the epic returned to `closed`, reopening child stories aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4 (S7) and 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab (S7.3) left the epic `closed` while the children were `in_progress`.\n\n## Expected\n`reopen` should carry the SAME parent-first cascade as `claim` / `transition open in_progress` (which pull a still-open/closed parent forward): reopening a child should reopen its transitive closed parents so the parent/child status invariant (a parent is never 'more closed' than its children) is preserved.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Reopening a child whose parent is closed reopens the parent (transitively to the root), in one atomic operation, mirroring the claim/transition parent-first cascade.\n- [ ] The parent/child status invariant is restored: it is impossible to end a reopen with a closed parent that has a non-closed child.\n- [ ] Held-out tests cover: reopen child under closed parent (parent reopens), reopen under already-open parent (no-op on parent), multi-level chain (all ancestors reopen), and concurrency (optimistic-concurrency mismatch surfaces exit 10, no partial cascade).\n- [ ] Docs/concurrency note updated to describe the reopen parent-first cascade alongside the existing claim/transition cascade.","id":"a392-f630-7b25-4b14","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"reopen lacks the parent-first cascade that claim/transition have, allowing a closed parent with an open child"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787170459974071001,"uuid":"e07ece13-d0fc-4aba-8f51-41584e6fb282"}